      <memberdef kind="function" id="classPatient_1af7b2fbbefcfa9f8be148faa6a92259e8" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::optional&lt; std::string &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::optional&lt; std::string &gt; Patient::getSqlGetVisitsStatement</definition>
        <argsstring>(pqxx::params &amp;params)</argsstring>
        <name>getSqlGetVisitsStatement</name>
        <qualifiedname>Patient::getSqlGetVisitsStatement</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>pqxx::params &amp;</type>
          <declname>params</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Builds the SELECT that lists all visits of this patient. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Resets <computeroutput>params</computeroutput>, binds the patient id held in the <ref refid="classData__t" kindref="compound">Data_t</ref> wrapper, and returns the query over <computeroutput>clinics_visits</computeroutput>. <ref refid="classController_1acd1d7cb00688b69469719ff7789f3cd9" kindref="member">Controller::GetVisits</ref> / GetVisitsAsync execute it with those same params and serialise the rows back to the caller. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bound parameters, cleared before the patient id is appended. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The <computeroutput>SELECT * FROM clinics_visits WHERE patient_id = $1;</computeroutput> statement. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para>The entity must hold a <ref refid="classData__t" kindref="compound">Data_t</ref> with an id. </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::bad_variant_access</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if the stored wrapper is not a <ref refid="classData__t" kindref="compound">Data_t</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::bad_optional_access</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if that wrapper has no id. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>These exceptions are not caught here; the controller&apos;s handler catches them. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
