    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A thin value type binding the generic Case/Entity CRUD machinery to one table. SQL generation is inherited; this class fixes the table name and overrides create authorisation: because a patient belongs directly to a clinic, the create payload&apos;s <computeroutput>clinic_id</computeroutput> is checked against <computeroutput>clinics</computeroutput> without the patient-table join used by the other <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref> types. This is also the only <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref> that builds a visits query; the controller uses it in GetVisits/GetVisitsAsync (guarded by <computeroutput>requires std::is_same&lt;T, <ref refid="classPatient" kindref="compound">Patient</ref>&gt;</computeroutput>). The static getPermissionsQueryFor* helpers are passed to <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> for api::v2::Case_t T. The type is registered as <ref refid="classClinicController" kindref="compound">ClinicController&lt;Patient&gt;</ref> under the <computeroutput>patients</computeroutput> serviceType, which also owns search and getvisits routes. Ownership: the wrapper is copied into <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> and is const thereafter; no mutable state and no locking of its own. Copy and move are explicitly deleted: create a fresh instance per operation. <simplesect kind="note"><para>No default constructor: <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> needs a data wrapper to build statements from. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref>, <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref>, <ref refid="classClinicController" kindref="compound">ClinicController</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
